ow (4) if they lie on a diagonal (constant c-r), and their distance from the diagonal's top-leftmost point is odd. I'm systematically checking against the provided test data to ensure this pattern holds universally and to identify any remaining cells with the value '6'.\n\n**Applying Diagonal Logic**\n\nI've confirmed my diagonal logic. Pixels transform to yellow (4) if they are on a diagonal where c-r is constant, and their position along that diagonal is odd. This accounts for the observed transformations and I am now focused on the remaining '6' values.\n\n",
